data-uid="5"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">ground cumin</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="6"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">sweet paprika</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="7"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">egg</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="8"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1 &frac12;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">kosher salt</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="9"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac12;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">black pepper</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="10"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac14;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">red pepper flakes</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">optional</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="11"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac14;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">fresh Italian parsley</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">chopped</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="12"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">olive oil</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">to use when shaping the kofta (or water)</span></li></ul></div></div>
<div id="recipe-83167-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-83167-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="83167"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-83167-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Place a fine mesh strainer over a bowl and set it aside. Using the large holes of a box grater, grate the onion*. Place the grated onion into the strainer. Using the back of a spoon, strain all of its juices. Transfer the onion to a large mixing bowl. Discard the juices.</span></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Chicken-Kofte-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Person grating onion and then straining its juices." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Chicken-Kofte-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Chicken-Kofte-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Chicken-Kofte-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Chicken-Kofte-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Chicken-Kofte.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Chicken-Kofte.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-83167-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Into that same bowl, add 1 lb ground chicken, &frac12; cup of panko breadcrumbs, 2 cloves of minced garlic, &frac14; teaspoon of baking soda, 1 teaspoon of ground cumin, 1 teaspoon of sweet paprika, 1 large egg, 1 &frac12; teaspoon of kosher salt, &frac12; teaspoon of black pepper, &frac14; teaspoon of red pepper flakes, and &frac14; of chopped fresh parsley.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ground-chicken-koftas-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="A collage of images showing the making of the chicken kofta mixture." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ground-chicken-koftas-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ground-chicken-koftas-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ground-chicken-koftas-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ground-chicken-koftas-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ground-chicken-koftas.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ground-chicken-koftas.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-83167-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Mix with clean hands until well combined.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83167-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Pour the olive oil into a small bowl. To shape the kofta, scoop about 2 tablespoons of the mixture, oil your hands lightly, and form into 10 oval patties (or your preferred shape). A cookie scoop works well for even portions.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Chicken-kofta-kabobs-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Person shaping chicken koftas and grilling them." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Chicken-kofta-kabobs-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Chicken-kofta-kabobs-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Chicken-kofta-kabobs-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Chicken-kofta-kabobs-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Chicken-kofta-kabobs.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Chicken-kofta-kabobs.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-83167-step-0-4" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Arrange the koftas on a platter, cover with plastic wrap, and let them rest at room temperature for 10-15 minutes before cooking.</span></div></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">Cooking On The Grill</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-83167-step-1-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Preheat a gas grill to medium-high heat. Clean the grates, then oil them using a paper towel dipped in oil.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83167-step-1-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Grill the kofta for 2-3 minutes for each side, turning often, until lightly golden brown and cooked through. They&rsquo;re ready when an instant-read thermometer inserted into the center registers 165&deg;F.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83167-step-1-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Transfer to a plate and let rest for 5-10 minutes before serving.</div></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">In The Oven</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-83167-step-2-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Preheat your oven to 375 &deg;F (191&deg;C). Line a baking sheet with parchment paper and set it aside.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83167-step-2-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Arrange the chicken koftas on the baking sheet and bake for 15 minutes, flipping them halfway through the cooking process for even baking.</span></div></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">On The Stove top</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-83167-step-3-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Heat a tablespoon of olive oil in a cast-iron skillet (or a large non-stick skillet) over medium high heat until shimmering.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83167-step-3-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Place the patties in the skillet, and cook undisturbed, for 2-3 minutes or until lightly golden brown. Continue to cook each side, turning every 2-3 minutes. It should take no more than 8 minutes to cook.* </span></div></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">In The Air Fryer</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-83167-step-4-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Preheat your air fryer to 375 &deg;F (191&deg;C). Lightly spray (or brush) it with oil. </span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83167-step-4-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Arrange the koftas in a single layer, leaving enough room between each patty for air to circulate.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83167-step-4-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Air fry for 12-13 minutes, turning them halfway through, until the center of a chicken kofta registers 165&deg;F (74 &deg;C) when inserted with a meat thermometer.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>
